0..77 Comment "// Definitions a Rust caller runs on its own values, and a Rust function they"
78..112 Comment "// call, admitted against its row."
113..115 Comment "//"
116..194 Comment "// The first direction: Rust holds the composed program and calls a definition"
195..273 Comment "// by name. The second: the `extern` block declares the Rust caller\'s `add` as"
274..351 Comment "// an operation of the interface `Boundary`, and `quadrupled` performs it. No"
352..427 Comment "// handler here answers it, so the run offers it to the Rust caller\'s host,"
428..507 Comment "// which calls its own `add`. The block names `add`\'s row, and its check admits"
508..582 Comment "// the declared types against the row under Rust\'s default layout. A `u32`"
583..657 Comment "// crosses as itself, and `by-layout.gandr` reads values by their layouts."
658..660 Comment "//"
661..737 Comment "// The Rust test composes this source, names each definition and calls it on"
738..815 Comment "// values it builds, then reads the answer back. Each `runs` item below makes"
816..893 Comment "// the same call from gandr, so both sides state one answer. `quadrupled` has"
894..949 Comment "// none, since only the Rust caller answers `Boundary`."
950..952 Comment "//"
953..1032 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/by-layout.gandr` — values crossing by their"
1033..1045 Comment "//   layouts"
1046..1121 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller"
1122..1200 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/boundary.gandr` — `admitBlock`, which the block\'s"
1201..1216 Comment "//   check runs"
1217..1294 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/function-row.gandr` — the function row an"
1295..1328 Comment "//   `extern` is admitted against"
1330..1404 Comment "// The boundary check reads `admitBlock` here, whatever the listing names."
